{"key":"enterprise/T1554","id":"T1554","name":"Compromise Host Software Binary","domain":"enterprise","level":"technique","parent_id":null,"tactics":["persistence"],"platforms":["ESXi","Linux","macOS","Windows"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem","virtualization"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may modify host software binaries to establish persistent access to systems. Software binaries/executables provide a wide range of system commands or services, programs, and libraries. Common software binaries are SSH clients, FTP clients, email clients, web browsers, and many other user or server applications. Adversaries may establish persistence though modifications to host software binaries. For example, an adversary may replace…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1554","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--960c3c86-1480-4d72-b4e0-8c242e84a5c5","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.706Z","source_object_version":"2.2","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0039","name":"File Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0039","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--2b3bfe19-d59a-460d-93bb-2f546adc2d2c","page":"telemetry/DC0039/"},{"id":"DC0061","name":"File Modification","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0061","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--84572de3-9583-4c73-aabd-06ea88123dd8","page":"telemetry/DC0061/"},{"id":"DC0016","name":"Module Load","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0016","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--c0a4a086-cc20-4e1e-b7cb-29d99dfa3fb1","page":"telemetry/DC0016/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0336","name":"Detect Compromise of Host Software Binaries","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0336","stix_id":"x-mitre-de